     "ruleId": "PRREV-4431-GHOST-BINDING-MSE-SPLIT",
     "level": "error",
     "message": {
      "text": "contracts/aprender/binding.yaml (edited by cf038d37f, this PR) now binds decision-tree-v1.yaml's mse_split to module_path aprender::tree::helpers, function compute_mse, status implemented. crates/aprender-core/src/tree/helpers.rs has no compute_mse; the real fn is pub(super) in regression_helpers.rs and is not re-exported through helpers. binding-allowlist.json does not name it. bindings_gate.rs::resolve_depth walks module_path::function through re-exports only, so this binding will not resolve and will be counted as a ghost (PV-ONT-028) the next time --gate bindings runs."
     },
     "locations": [
      { "physicalLocation": { "artifactLocation": { "uri": "contracts/aprender/binding.yaml" }, "region": { "startLine": 188 } } }
     ],
     "properties": {
      "grounding": "measured",
      "command": ["grep", "-rn", "fn compute_mse", "crates/aprender-core/src/tree/"],
      "exit_code": 0,
      "stdout_sha256": "01cc86128eb832a8c559d84e428caf80f6c92bbe86ca37adac6560ea19df75a5",
      "failure_scenario": "pv obligations check-bindings / pv lint --gate bindings run against this tree counts mse_split as an unresolved, unallowlisted ghost and fails the bindings gate (PV-ONT-028), or — if merged unnoticed — silently drops mse_split's implemented-status guarantee, so a later regression to compute_mse's MSE-split math has no contract holding it.",
      "precision_class": "advisory",
      "rationale_for_class": "Real, measured, and independently reproduced (agy found the same binding; see antigravity run), but not one of the six mechanical B1-B6 classes in SS7, so it cannot itself force BLOCK; it is reported for the human/CI merge decision."
     }
